    <data key="g_citation">[&apos;R. Michalski, S. Palus, and P. Kazienko, &quot;Matching organizational structure and social network extracted from email communication.&quot; In Lecture Notes in Business Information Processing 87, 197-206 (2011), http://www.ii.pwr.edu.pl/~michalski/publications/pub_2011_bis.pdf&apos;]</data>
    <data key="g_description">A network of emails among employee email addresses at a mid-sized manufacturing company. Each directed edge represents an email sent from address i to address j. Edges are timestamped, and occurred over a 6 month period in an unspecified year.</data>
    <data key="g_konect_meta">category: Communication 
code: RA
name: Manufacturing emails
description: Employee–employee email
entity-names: employee
extr: radoslaw
url: http://www.ii.pwr.wroc.pl/~michalski/index.php?content=datasets#manufacturing
long-description: This is the internal email communication network between employees of a mid-sized manufacturing company. The network is directed and nodes represent employees. The left node represents the sender and the right node represents the recipient. Edges between two nodes are individual emails. 
relationship-names: email
cite: konect:radoslaw
timeiso: 2010-01-01/2010-09-30
tags: #loop
</data>
    <data key="g_konect_readme">Manufacturing emails network, part of the Koblenz Network Collection
===========================================================================

This directory contains the TSV and related files of the radoslaw_email network: This is the internal email communication network between employees of a mid-sized manufacturing company. The network is directed and nodes represent employees. The left node represents the sender and the right node represents the recipient. Edges between two nodes are individual emails. 


More information about the network is provided here: 
http://konect.cc/networks/radoslaw_email

Files: 
    meta.radoslaw_email -- Metadata about the network 
    out.radoslaw_email -- The adjacency matrix of the network in whitespace-separated values format, with one edge per line
      The meaning of the columns in out.radoslaw_email are: 
        First column: ID of from node 
        Second column: ID of to node
        Third column (if present): weight or multiplicity of edge
        Fourth column (if present):  timestamp of edges Unix time
        Third column: edge weight
        Fourth column: timestamp of the edge


Use the following References for citation:

